# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirects.
#
# Line 1 forwards the API to the backend, so the browser stays on one origin and
# no CORS configuration is needed. The frontend calls "/api" as a relative path
# (frontend/src/lib/api.ts), so this is what makes production match development,
# where vite.config.ts proxies the same path.
#
# Replace prism-api.onrender.com with your own backend host.
#
# Line 2 is the React Router fallback. Without it, opening /figur/1 directly
# returns a 404, because the host looks for a file named figur/1 and there is
# none. The 200 status makes it a rewrite rather than a redirect, so the URL in
# the address bar does not change.
/api/*  https://nodus-0qo0.onrender.com/api/:splat  200
/*      /index.html                                200
